IMPORT prelude

-- Moneylenders Act 2008 (Singapore) -- who is a moneylender (ss 2, 3), unlicensed moneylending and its consequences for the
-- loan (ss 5, 19), unpermitted charges (s 35), the interest cap (s 36), reopening unfair loans (s 37), harassment (s 47),
-- and using children (s 49).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/MA2008.txt
-- (amendments to Act 32 of 2024).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 18 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the borrower's position and
-- the loan-shark offences. Not encoded: licensing procedure and conditions (Part 2 beyond ss 5 and 19), freezing proceeds
-- (Part 2A), advertising and disclosure duties (ss 29 to 34), audit and inspection, the credit bureau (Part 3A), and the
-- rules (which fix the interest cap and permitted fees; not retrieved).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Moneylenders Act 2008 -- borrowers`

§§ `2, 3 -- who is a moneylender`

-- s 3: "Any person, other than an excluded moneylender, who lends a sum of money in consideration of a LARGER SUM being repaid
-- is PRESUMED, until the contrary is proved, to be a moneylender." s 2: an "unlicensed moneylender" is a person presumed to be
-- one under s 3 who is not a licensee or exempt. "Excluded moneylender" includes banks and MAS-regulated lenders, credit
-- co-operatives, licensed pawnbrokers, and a person who lends SOLELY to employees, accredited investors, or companies and LLPs.
--
-- A friend who lends $1,000 and asks for $1,100 back is presumed to be a moneylender and so an "unlicensed moneylender",
-- unless they prove they do not carry on a business of moneylending.
DECLARE Lender HAS
    `is an excluded moneylender` IS A BOOLEAN
    `lent for a larger sum to be repaid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `proved no business of moneylending` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is licensed or exempt` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the lender` IS A Lender
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lender is presumed a moneylender` IF
        `the lender`'s `lent for a larger sum to be repaid`
    AND NOT `the lender`'s `is an excluded moneylender`
    AND NOT `the lender`'s `proved no business of moneylending`

GIVEN `the lender` IS A Lender
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lender is an unlicensed moneylender` IF
        `the lender is presumed a moneylender` `the lender`
    AND NOT `the lender`'s `is licensed or exempt`

§§ `19 -- unlicensed moneylending`

-- s 19(1): carrying on or assisting unlicensed moneylending -- an individual, a fine of $30,000 to $300,000 AND imprisonment up
-- to 4 years (7 on repeat); (2) and up to 6 strokes of the cane (12 on repeat). (5): "assists" includes collecting repayments,
-- and handling funds or "engag[ing] in a banking transaction" for the lender -- letting an account be used.
-- (3): "the contract for the loan, and the guarantee or security ... is UNENFORCEABLE; and (b) any money paid by or on behalf of
-- the unlicensed moneylender under the contract for the loan is NOT RECOVERABLE in any court of law."
--
-- The borrower from a loan shark owes nothing the law will enforce -- not the interest, and not the principal either.
GIVEN `the lender` IS A Lender, `amount lent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount the lender can recover in court` MEANS
    IF `the lender is an unlicensed moneylender` `the lender` THEN 0 ELSE `amount lent`

DECLARE Assistance IS ONE OF
    `collecting repayments`
    `letting one's bank account receive the lender's money`
    `running errands unconnected with the loans`

GIVEN `the act` IS AN Assistance, `knew or had reasonable grounds to believe` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act assists unlicensed moneylending` IF
        `knew or had reasonable grounds to believe`
    AND CONSIDER `the act`
        WHEN `running errands unconnected with the loans` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `35, 36 -- charges and the interest cap for licensees`

-- s 35(3): any charge beyond the prescribed permitted fees "(a) is not recoverable ...; (b) if so paid, is recoverable as a
-- debt due to the borrower ...; and (c) if not recovered, is to be set off against the outstanding amount".
-- s 36(1): a licensee must not contract for interest or late interest above the prescribed maximum. (3): if it does, "(a) the
-- contract is UNENFORCEABLE against the borrower or any surety; (b) ... any guarantee or security [is unenforceable]; and (c) any
-- money paid by or on behalf of the licensee under the contract is NOT RECOVERABLE".
--
-- A licensed lender whose rate is a fraction over the cap loses not only the excess interest but the whole loan, principal
-- included. The caps themselves are in rules, not retrieved; the rate is a parameter.
DECLARE LicensedLoan HAS
    `contract interest rate per month` IS A NUMBER
    `prescribed maximum rate per month` IS A NUMBER
    `principal` IS A NUMBER
    `unpermitted charges paid` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the loan` IS A LicensedLoan
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the loan exceeds the cap` IF
    `the loan`'s `contract interest rate per month` GREATER THAN `the loan`'s `prescribed maximum rate per month`

GIVEN `the loan` IS A LicensedLoan
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the principal the licensee can recover` MEANS
    IF `the loan exceeds the cap` `the loan` THEN 0 ELSE `the loan`'s `principal`

GIVEN `the loan` IS A LicensedLoan
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the borrower's claim back for charges` MEANS
    `the loan`'s `unpermitted charges paid`

§§ `37 -- reopening a licensee's loan`

-- s 37(1): the court "IS TO reopen the transaction" if satisfied "that the interest or late interest charged ... is EXCESSIVE AND
-- that the transaction is UNCONSCIONABLE OR SUBSTANTIALLY UNFAIR". (4): a borrower may apply even before repayment is due, even
-- if the licensee's own claim is time-barred, "despite any provision or agreement to the contrary".
--
-- Excessive interest alone is not enough; the transaction must also be unconscionable or substantially unfair.
GIVEN `interest is excessive` IS A BOOLEAN, `unconscionable or substantially unfair` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court must reopen the loan` IF
    `interest is excessive` AND `unconscionable or substantially unfair`

§§ `47 -- harassment by loan sharks`

-- s 47(1): where an UNLICENSED moneylender, or anyone on its behalf ((2), presumed under (6) for anyone harassing in connection
-- with a demand), uses threatening, abusive or insulting words or behaviour, or "commits any act likely to cause alarm or
-- annoyance" to the borrower, surety, their family, "or any other person", in connection with a loan -- imprisonment up to 5
-- years (and 2 to 9 on repeat) with fines, and (3) caning: mandatory 3 to 6 strokes if property was damaged, 5 to 8 if hurt
-- was caused, 6 to 12 if both; more on repeat. (7): "damage" includes defacing with paint, "coffee, soya sauce or any other
-- delible or indelible substance", posters, or fire.
--
-- s 47 reaches only UNLICENSED moneylenders. A licensed moneylender who harasses a borrower is outside this section; whatever
-- remedy there is lies elsewhere.
DECLARE Harassment HAS
    `by or for an unlicensed moneylender` IS A BOOLEAN
    `threatening, abusive, or likely to cause alarm or annoyance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `damaged property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `caused hurt` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a repeat offence` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the act` IS A Harassment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is a section 47 offence` IF
    `the act`'s `by or for an unlicensed moneylender` AND `the act`'s `threatening, abusive, or likely to cause alarm or annoyance`

GIVEN `the act` IS A Harassment
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum strokes of the cane` MEANS
    IF NOT `the act is a section 47 offence` `the act` THEN 0
    ELSE IF `the act`'s `is a repeat offence`
         THEN (IF `the act`'s `damaged property` AND `the act`'s `caused hurt` THEN 9
               ELSE IF `the act`'s `caused hurt` THEN 6
                    ELSE IF `the act`'s `damaged property` THEN 5 ELSE 0)
         ELSE (IF `the act`'s `damaged property` AND `the act`'s `caused hurt` THEN 6
               ELSE IF `the act`'s `caused hurt` THEN 5
                    ELSE IF `the act`'s `damaged property` THEN 3 ELSE 0)

GIVEN `the act` IS A Harassment
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum strokes of the cane` MEANS
    IF NOT `the act is a section 47 offence` `the act` THEN 0
    ELSE IF `the act`'s `is a repeat offence`
         THEN (IF `the act`'s `damaged property` AND `the act`'s `caused hurt` THEN 18
               ELSE IF `the act`'s `caused hurt` THEN 12
                    ELSE IF `the act`'s `damaged property` THEN 10 ELSE 12)
         ELSE (IF `the act`'s `damaged property` AND `the act`'s `caused hurt` THEN 12
               ELSE IF `the act`'s `caused hurt` THEN 8
                    ELSE 6)

DECLARE Defacement IS ONE OF
    `paint`
    `coffee or soya sauce`
    `a poster or notice`
    `fire`
    `a polite letter`

GIVEN `the means` IS A Defacement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the means counts as damage to property` IF
    CONSIDER `the means`
    WHEN `a polite letter` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `49 -- using children`

-- s 49(1): a person aged 21 or over who causes or procures a person under 16 to commit an offence under s 19 or s 47 --
-- up to 7 years (s 19) or 2 to 9 years (s 47), with fines and up to 12 strokes.
GIVEN `age of the adult` IS A NUMBER, `age of the child` IS A NUMBER, `procured the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the adult commits the section 49 offence` IF
        `procured the offence`
    AND `age of the adult` AT LEAST 21
    AND `age of the child` LESS THAN 16
